<#assign metaDescription = "Denebola builds online learning infrastructure for schools and universities. Learn about our mission and approach." />
<#assign canonicalPath = "/about.html" />
<#assign navActive = "about" />
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<#include "partials/head.ftl">
<body class="page-about">
<#include "partials/nav.ftl">

  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-header">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Built for the people who run schools</h1>
        <p class="page-header__lead">
          Denebola is named after a star in the constellation Leo — a fixed point
          institutions can navigate by. That's the idea behind the platform too.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>Our mission</h2>
        <p>
          Schools and universities run on more systems than they should have to:
          a video tool for classes, a spreadsheet for fees, a separate form for
          feedback, and no easy way to see how it all connects. Denebola exists
          to bring that back together — one platform for live learning, school
          administration, feedback, and the data behind all of it.
        </p>

        <h2>How we approach it</h2>
        <p>
          We build for the administrators, teachers, and finance staff who use
          these tools every day, not just for the decision-makers who buy them.
          That means workflows that match how institutions actually operate,
          data that's easy to act on, and a platform that stays out of the way
          when it isn't needed.
        </p>

        <h2>What we're building toward</h2>
        <p>
          Live class management, fee and school management, and feedback tools
          are the foundation. On top of that, we're investing in data science
          and AI that turns everyday institutional data — attendance, fees,
          engagement — into decisions leadership can act on early, not after
          the fact.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section cta-banner">
      <div class="wrap cta-banner__inner">
        <div>
          <h2>Want to talk to the team?</h2>
          <p>We're happy to walk through what Denebola looks like for your institution.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact.html" class="btn btn--primary btn--large">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

<#include "partials/footer.ftl">
<#include "partials/scripts.ftl">
</body>
</html>
